for sure  uh  the new information technologies are  fragmenting  monolithic  social  consensus  and what i mean by that is for instance  when i was a kid  on friday night  between 6 and 7  [Music]  gunsmoke was on  cbs  you could have fairly high confidence  that 30 percent of the american  population was tuned in  in other words that as a culture we were  all  at the same moment sharing this  experience  now you know  people follow their own interests and so  there is enormous fragmentation and this  thing i call the balkanization of  epistemology goes along with that now we  aren't either catholics lutherans or  jews  now there's a vast  smorgasbord of possibilities even the uh  you know and it continues to fragment  almost down to the individual level  so for instance  i used to be a news hound  once that meant  hourly  newscasts  now whenever i need to know what's going  on in the world whether that's twice a  day or twice an hour i just go to the  top stories page at yahoo and and it's  delivered to me so there is a tendency  for us to excentrify  and and island ourselves but in a way  that is is the precondition for uh  creativity that what we give back to the  society based on our  personal ex  pursuit of our own eccentric agendas  what we give back to the society then  are diverse insights  new understandings that can't arise in  an environment  of consensus  as to then  what your question implies the the the  counter flow of that how shall we build  than  uh  a culture  in a way i think that what we're seeing  is the end of culture  that culture  is a  xenophobic  paranoid notion  our culture means our consensus how we  think how we do things the foods we eat  at the end of culture at the end of that  road at the dissolution of culture what  you have is enormous  diversity  one other next week i'll be spending a  few days in manhattan  one of the reasons i love that town so  much  is because you never know  what's next and you never know who's  next and through the genius of its  verticality  the rich cannot escape the culture of  the streets and the streets are not free  from having the very wealthy the very  rich  move among them i mean  so everybody is confronted with  everybody else and it's being confronted  by people you never imagined you would  be confronted with  that teaches you tolerance  you know if you if you've never had to  deal with people of a different  ethnicity or class or gender preference  well then you're just free to have any  kind of paranoid fantasies you want  about how those people operate but if  you are constantly in the presence of  diversity you begin to become  sophisticated this is what civilized  means it means you know your jaw doesn't  drop when somebody walks by  with a hairstyle or a fashion or a  manner unfamiliar to you you make  a place for that  and it's xenophobia that drives warfare  territoriality search for ideological  purity pogroms inquisitions  so forth and so on so uh and it's very  psychedelic to tolerate  this diversity and what psychedelics  teach you i think is that underneath all  these expressions of diversity there's  another human soul  a human animal and there there is great  homogeneity  uh  one of the  concepts that's probably going to take a  real pounding as we move into the future  is the preciousness of the individual  personality the preciousness of the  individual ego i can imagine a future  where  bodies are nodal points in a web and you  just settle where it's comfortable for a  while and then move on and make room for  someone else  and you don't have to own a body and you  don't have to  you know have one personality one body  you can become context dependent and as  avatars  flourish and this sort of thing you all  know what i mean by avatars i mean  these  software constructs that are how you  appear to other people on the internet  you know and these will be your  personalities well eventually we'll all  have 50 or 60 avatars hanging in our  virtual closet  and you'll get up in the morning and  decide you know  do i want to be a meteorite the queen of  england  a german pop star  or  whatever and mood will  and diversity will rule it's all about  boundary dissolution plasticity  transformation and the replacing of  solid and defined entities with more  amorphous and self-transforming  entities  perhaps we will become self-transforming  machine learners at least in some of our  avatars  [Music]  you

